PARITY (web OfflineBanner.tsx → native)
  Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder seam, no networking in the view):
    useOnlineStatus  → OfflineBannerSource emits OfflineBannerInput (the connectivity reading — the web
                       getConnectionStatus() 'online'|'offline' boolean — plus the probe's load/error state
                       and the freshness axis). The production MonitoredOfflineBannerSource subscribes to
                       NWPathMonitor (the device analogue of navigator.onLine + the lib/resilience
                       online/offline broadcaster); the view never reads connectivity directly.
    useTranslation   → OfflineBannerStrings P1/S10 facade (every literal keyed; no English in code).
  Composition: warning-toned alert card (web variant="warning" → statusWarning) + wifi.slash icon
               (web <WifiOff/>), the "You're offline" title (bodySm semibold) + the "Showing cached data…"
               reassurance (caption). role="status"/aria-live="polite" → one combined VoiceOver element with
               the pre-composed accessibilitySummary + .isStaticText. Web `if (online) return null` →
               the friendly "You're connected" empty leaf (never a blank box, P4 contract).
  i18n keys (web → catalog): pwa.offline.title ("You're offline"), pwa.offline.banner ("Showing cached
               data. New requests will retry when you reconnect.") — both present + asserted by the
               OfflineBannerCopy.webSourceKeys parity test; + native P4 leaf chrome (loading/online/error)
               + freshness (offline/stale chips + a11y) keys.
  States rendered (every one, no hidden surface):
    loading  -> OfflineBannerLoadingView (skeleton banner chrome)
    empty    -> OfflineBannerOnlineView (web null branch → friendly connected card)
    error    -> OfflineBannerErrorView (web QueryError peer + retry)
    offline  -> OfflineBannerCard + freshness chip "Offline" (live reading)
    stale    -> OfflineBannerCard + freshness chip "Stale" + one-shot auto re-probe on the stale edge

